398,"Allah.; enjoined As-Saldt (the prayer), when H errjoined it, it was twof Rak'a only (i every Saldf) both when in residence of during journey. Then ls-Saldt offere during journey remained the same, b (the Rak'a of) As-Saldt fnon travellers were increased"
399,"Indeed! In the Messengof Allah (Muhammad d- , +r, crrrd-r- ) yof have a good example tof follow (V.33:21) . Nanated Anas (bin Mdlik +.u' I offered fou Rak'a of Zuh (midday praywith the Prophett d- r"
400,"On the day of Badr, the Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Who will go and see what has happened to Abu Jahl?"" Ibn Mas`ud went and found that the two sons of 'Afra had struck him fatally. `Abdullah bin Mas`ud got hold of his beard and said, ""'Are you Abu Jahl?"" He replied, ""Can there be a man more superior to one whom his own folk have killed (or you have killed)?"""
401,"r : W travelled with the Prophett d-, eir' ^r from Al-Madina tof Makka and offere twof Rak'a [fevery Saldt Qxayer)] t we returned tof Al-Madina. I aske ""Did yo stay fsome days 6. .Salr of travelters and iS fa Makka?"" He replied"
402,"l offered Saldt (prayer) with the Prophett d- r, ,r- , Ab Bak .u, c and 'Umare i 4 c4 at Mina and it was twof Rak'a.'Uthmdn d' 4J164 in the early days of his caliphate did the same"
403,"The Prophet (ﷺ) led us in a prayer and then got up on the pulpit and said, In your prayer and bowing"
404,"Zurara b. Aufa said that Sa'd b. Hisham divorced his wife, and then proceeded to Medina to sell his property, and the rest of the hadith is the same"
405,"Anas b. Malik reported that his grandmother, Mulaika, invited the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to a dinner which she had prepared. He (the Holy Prophet) ate out of that and then said:Stand up so that I should observe prayer (in order to bless) you Anas b. Malik said: I stood up on a mat (belonging to us) which had turned dark on account of its long use. I sprinkled water over it (in order to soften it), and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood upon it, and I and an orphan formed a row behind him (the Holy Prophet) and the old woman was behind us, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in two rak'ahs of prayer and then went back"
406,"that he had seen the Prophett d, ..rr , p-, praying Nawdfil at night on the bac of his Rdhila (mount) on a journey facing whatevdirection it took"
407,"""Narrated `Ata' bin Yasar:I asked Zaid bin Thabit about prostration on which he said that he had recited An-Najm before the Prophet, yet he (the Prophet) had not performed a prostration"""
408,"Ibn Samura al-'Adawi reported:I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) say, and he then narrated (the above-mentioned hadith)"
409,"I saw Allah's Messengof ,1 l-:"
410,"Husain b. 'Abd al-Rahman reported:I was with Sa'id b. Jubair when he said: Who amongst you saw a star shooting last night? I said: It was I; then I said: I was in fact not (busy) in prayer, but was stung by a scorpion (and that is the reason why I was awake and had a glimpse of the shooting star). He said: Then what did you do? I said: I practised charm. He said: What urged you to do this? I said: (I did this according to the implied suggestion) of the hadith which al-Shu'ba narrated. He said: What did al-Shu'ba narrate to you? I said: Buraida b. Husaib al-Aslami narrated to us. The charm is of no avail except in case of the (evil influence) of an eye or the sting of a scorpion. He said: He who acted according to what he had heard (from the Holy Prophet) acted rightly, but Ibn 'Abbas narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: There were brought before me the peoples and I saw an apostle and a small group (of his followers) along with him, another (apostle) and one or two persons (along with him) and (still another) apostle having no one with him. When a very large group was brought to me I conceived as if it were my Ummah. Then it was said to me: It is Moses and his people. You should look at the horizon, and I saw a very huge group. It was again said to me: See the other side of the horizon, and there was (also) a very huge group. It was said to me: This is your Ummah, and amongst them there were seventy thousand persons who would be made to enter Paradise without rendering any account and without (suffering) any torment. He then stood up and went to his house. Then the people began to talk about the people who would be admitted to Paradise without rendering any account and without (suffering) any torment. Some of them said: They may be those who (have had the good fortune of living) in the company of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and some of them said: They be those who were born in Islam and did not associate anything with Allah. Some people mentioned other things. Thereupon came forth the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) before them and he said: What was that which you were talking about? They informed him. He said: They are those persons who neither practise charm, nor ask others to practise it, nor do they take omens, and repose their trust in their Lord. Upon this 'Ukkasha b. Mihsan stood up and said: Supplicate for me that He should make me one among them. Upon this he (Messenger of Allah) said: Thou are one among them. Then another man stood up and said: Supplicate before Allah that He should make me one among them. Upon this he said: 'Ukkisha has preceded you"
411,"Alqama b. Waqqas reported:I asked 'A'isha how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did in the two rak'ahs as he (observed them) sitting. She said: He would recite (the Qur'an) in them, and when he intended to bow, he would stand up and then bowed"
412,"Yo should not give away a part of you Saldt (prayer) tof Satand by thinking that it is necessary tof depart (aftfinishing the prayer) from one's right side only; I have seen the Prophett d* .-r, .u, ,r.- often departing from the left side. It is disliked tof offe the Nawdjil (optional) Saht (prayer) aftthe call mak(Mu'adh-dhin) has started the call flqhma"
413,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saw a person sitting aloof and not praying with the people. He asked him, O so and so! What prevented you from offering the prayer with the people?"" He replied"
414,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, If anyone of you enters a mosque"
415,"I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) in a Ghazwa (Military Expedition) and my camel was slow and exhausted. The Prophet came up to me and said, O Jabir."" I replied"
416,"Abu Huraira reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) used to observe, silence for a short while between the takbir (at the time of opening the prayer) and the recitation of the Qur'an. I said to him:Messenger of Allah, for whom I would give my father and mother in ransom, what do you recite during your period of silence between the takbir and the recitation? He said: I say (these words): O Allah"
417,"Narrated Ibn Abi Laila * Only Umm Hani told us that she had seen the Prophett *,r.*r, ur,r. offering the Duha (forenoon prayer). She said, On the day of the conquest of Makka"
418,"Tof observe Saftm (fast) three days every (lunar) month, tof offe the Duha prayer, and tof offWit before sleeping. Preference of the twof Rak'a Sunna of the Faj (morning) prayand exhortation tof ot. . Nanated Hafsa rt,Jrt se:: Whe the Mu'adhdhin pronounced the Adhdn fFajr(morning)prayerandthedaw became evident,theProphettd-l+r,.l .;- would offa twof Rakia lieghtpray (Sunna) before the lqdmi in compulsory (congregational) Sal (prayer)"
419,"""Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""By Him in Whose Hands my life is, none of you will have faith till he loves me more than his father and his children."""
420,"rr : The Prophett p:4,uru_r. us€d tooffertw light Rak'a between the Adhdn and the 4ama of the Fai (moming) praye"
421,"Abu Burda b. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari reported:'Abdullah b. Umar said to me: Did you hear anything from your father narrating something from the messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the time on Friday? I said: Yes, I heard him say from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (these words): It is between the time when the Imam sits down and the end of the prayer"""
422,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Faith (Belief) consists of more than sixty branches (i.e. parts). And Haya (This term ""Haya"" covers a large number of concepts which are to be taken together; amongst them are self respect, modesty, bashfulness, and scruple, etc.) is a part of faith."""
423,"twof Rak'a aftMaghrib (evening),'Isha' (late evening) and Jumu'a (Friday) prayers. Those of the Maghrib and 'Isha' were offered in his house. It is allowed tof offe NawfrJil (optional) prayers standing sitting and tof offsome part of it standing sitting"
424,I did not see the Prophett p- r.r reciting (tl : Qur'dn) in the night praywhile sitting except when he became old
425,"Allah's Messenger-: -t, ar',r- (in his last days used tof perform Saldt (prayer) sitting He would recite while sitting, and when thrity forty Verses remained from the recitation, he would stand up and recite them while standing and then he would bow and prostrate. He used tof dof the same in the second Rak'a. Afte finishing the prayhe used tof look a me, and if I was awake he would talk tof me and if I was asleep, he would lie down. Night praye (Tahajjud) and the numbere of the Rak'a which the Prophett offered during the night, and tof offone Rak'a as Witr, and one Rak'a praye is perfectly correct. . Nanated Ab Salma bin 'Abd Rahmdn: I asked'Aisha ti.- dlt sisabo As-Saldt (the prayer) of Allah's Messeng& tr, or, during the mont of Ramadan. She said, Allah's Messenger-t 4'.r"
426,"I asked `Aisha, ""How is the prayer of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) during the month of Ramadan."" She said, ""Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) never exceeded eleven rak`at in Ramadan or in other months; he used to offer four rak`at-- do not ask me about their beauty and length, then four rak`at, do not ask me about their beauty and length, and then three rak`at."" Aisha further said, ""I said, 'O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! Do you sleep before offering the witr prayer?' He replied, 'O `Aisha! My eyes sleep but my heart remains awake'!"""
427,"Abu Burda b. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari reported:'Abdullah b. Umar said to me: Did you hear anything from your father narrating something from the messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the time on Friday? I said: Yes, I heard him say from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (these words): It is between the time when the Imam sits down and the end of the prayer"""
428,"I asked 'Aisha t i. !)t 6i) about the night praye of the Prophett -.t,rn "
429,"In my house he (Prophett p r,.l' /- ) neve passed the last hours of the night but sleeping"
430,"`Aisha said, ""We set out with the Prophet (ﷺ) in his last Hajj. Some of us intended to perform `Umra while others Hajj. When we reached Mecca, Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, 'Those who had assumed the lhram for `Umra and had not brought the Hadi should finish his lhram and whoever had assumed the Ihram for `Umra and brought the Hadi should not finish the Ihram till he has slaughtered his Hadi and whoever had assumed the lhram for Hajj should complete his Hajj."" `Aisha further said, ""I got my periods (menses) and kept on menstruating till the day of `Arafat, and I had assumed the Ihram for `Umra only (Tamattu`). The Prophet (ﷺ) ordered me to undo and comb my head hair and assume the lhram for Hajj only and leave the `Umra. I did the same till I completed the Hajj. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) sent `Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakr with me and ordered me to perform `Umra from at-Tan`im in lieu of the missed `Umra."""
431,Allah's Messengd-r.+ d
432,"Once a person asked Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) (ﷺ) about the night prayer. Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) replied, ""The night prayer is offered as two Rak`at followed by two Rak`at and so on and if anyone is afraid of the approaching dawn (Fajr prayer) he should pray one Rak`ah and this will be a Witr for all the Rak`at which he has prayed before."""
433,"The Prophett d-r,r"
434,"A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
435,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There are angels coming to you in succession at night"
436,"Once in the middle of the night, AllAh's Messenger-:,*.l ,- weflt out and prayed in the mosque and some men prayed with him. The next morning the people spoke about it and sof more people gathered and prayed with him (in the second night). They circulated the news in the morning, and so, on the third night the numbere of people increased greattly. Allah's Messenge l+ 4 -u .-r.. calr€ out and they prayed behind him. On the fourth night the mosque was sof crowded by the PeoPle till it could not accommodate them. Allah's Messeng&.J"" . came out only fthe Faj (morning) prayand when he finished the prayer"
437,"Hafsa reported:When the dawn appeared, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) observed two rak'ahs (of Sunnah prayers)"
438,"It has been narrated on the authority of Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari who said:A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: My riding beast has been killed, so give me some animal to ride upon. He (the Holy Prophet) said: I have none with me. A man said: Messenger of Allah, I can guide him to one who will provide him with a riding beast. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: One who guides to something good has a reward similar to that of its doer"
439,"Narrated Ibn ,Abb6s ,..1. {u djJ The Saldt (prayer) of the Prophett .r,, d- r used tof be of thirteen Rak'a"
440,"Whenever the Prophet (ﷺ) offered the night (Tahajjud) prayer, he used to say, O Allah! All the Praises are for You; You are the Light of the Heavens and the Earth. And all the Praises are for You; You are the Keeper of the Heavens and the Earth. All the Praises are for You; You are the Lord of the Heavens and the Earth and whatever is therein. You are the Truth"
441,"My father said, ""Once I was in the company of the Prophet (ﷺ) on a journey and I dashed to take off his Khuffs (socks made from thick fabric or leather). He ordered me to leave them as he had put them after performing ablution. So he passed wet hands over them."
442,"It rvas mentioned before the Prophett d- .+J, , that there was a mand whof slept the night till morning (afte sunrise). The Prophett p- qr- .ur;- said. He is a mand in whose ears (ear) Satand had urinated"""
443,"That one night Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) visited him and Fatima, the daughter of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said to them, Won 't you offer (night) prayer?.. `Ali added: I said"
444,"A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
445,"*.lr,-r- said, Offe some of you Saldt (prayer) (Nawdfit at home"
446,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, The example of the one who celebrates the Praises of his Lord (Allah) in comparison to the one who does not celebrate the Praises of his Lord"
447,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) made a small room in the month of Ramadan (Sa`id said, I think that Zaid bin Thabit said that it was made of a mat"") and he prayed there for a few nights"
448,"or, entered t he said, What is this rope?"" The people said"
449,"Abu Salama is reported to have said. I came to 'A'isha. I said:O mother, inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She said: His (night prayer) in Ramadan and (during other months) was thirteen rak'ahs at night including two rak'ahs of fajr"
450,"I proceeded till I entered upon `Umar (and while I was sitting there), his gate-keeper Yarfa came to him and said,  `Uthman"
451,"The Prophett d- q .lrur- heard a mand reciting the Qur'and in the mosque at night. The Prophett .l-r..r, o said, ''May Allah .l' bestow His Mercy on him, as he has reminded me of such and such Verses of such and such Sftrah, which missed"
452,Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said. While I was sleeping
453,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, It is a bad thing that some of you say"
454,This hadith has been transmitted by Ibrahim b. Sa'd b. Malik on the authority of his father
455,"Allah's Messengd-r.+.r ,-r- said, Allah ;'-"
456,"Abu Huraira said, The Prophet (ﷺ) said"
457,"I saw Allah's Messeng& qr,.r r- on the day of the conquest of Makka ovhis she-camel"
458,"A mand recited Sfirat Al-Kahf his prayer) and in the house there was (riding) animal which got frighten and started jumping. The mand finish his Saldt (prayer) with Tasltm, b behold! A mist a cloud hovered ov him. He informed the Prophett .*b ^r d-. of that and the Prophett p1+ . said"
459,"The hadith of Usayd ibn Hudayr, who said: ""While he was reciting Surat al-Baqarah at night, and his horse was tied beside him, the horse began to move about. He fell silent, and it fell silent. He recited again, and the horse moved about. He fell silent, and the horse fell silent. Then he recited again, and the horse moved about. He turned away, and his son Yahya was near it. He feared it might trample him. When he pulled him back, he raised his head to the sky until he could no longer see it. In the morning, he informed the Prophet, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him, who said: 'Recite, O Ibn Hudayr! Recite, O Ibn Hudayr!' He said: 'I feared, O Messenger of Allah, that it would trample Yahya, for he was near it. So I raised my head and turned to him. I raised my head to the sky and saw something like a canopy with what resembled lamps in it, rising until I could no longer see it.' The Prophet said: 'Do you know what that was?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Those were the angels who drew near to your voice. Had you continued reciting, the people would have seen them in the morning, and they would not have hidden themselves from them.'"""
460,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, The example of a Believer who recites the Qur'an"
461,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Such a person as recites the Qur'an and masters it by heart, will be with the noble righteous scribes (in Heaven). And such a person exerts himself to learn the Qur'an by heart, and recites it with great difficulty, will have a double reward."""
462,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said to Ubai, ""Allah has ordered me to recite to you: 'Those who disbelieve (Surat-al- Bayina 98).' "" Ubai said, ""Has He mentioned my name?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Yes."" On hearing this, Ubai started weeping."
463,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said (to me), Recite the Qur'an to me."" I said"
464,"recited Sftrat Yfisuf. A mand said (tof him), It was not revealed in this way."" Then Ibn Mas'0d said"
465,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, If one recites the last two verses of Surat al-Baqarah at night"
466,"2 I The Prophett 4--, {+1, d-r- said, Not tof wish tof be the like of except the like of twof (persons): a mand whom Allah t"
467,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Do not wish to be like anybody except in two cases: The case of a man whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it in the right way"
468,"I heard Hishim bin Hiz reciting Sfirat Al-Furqdn in a w different tof that of mine. Alld Messeng&r.+.r',.r- had taught i me (in a different way). Sof I was ab tof quarrel with him (during the praye but I waited till he finished, then I t his garment round his neck and sei him by it and brought, him tof Alld Messengp rJ, r- and said"
469,Abu Huraira reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:I shall be pre-eminent amongst the descendants of Adam on the Day of Resurrection and I will be the first intercessor and the first whose intercession will be accepted (by Allah)
470,"Narrated Ab Wa'il of o i A mand came tof Ibn Mas'0d and said, I recited the Mufassal (Sfirah) at night in one Rak'a."" Ibn Mas'0d said"
471,"The Prophett rq r+.x ul- used tof , 6. fne noot of tne Sa& of tmvelten anO i recite: 'Fahal min muddafrir' (then there any that will remembreceiv admonition?) (Sfirah 54)"
472,"Th companions of 'Abdull6h (bin Mas'0d came tof Abi Ad-Darad6', (and befo they arrived at his home), we looke fthem and found them. Then h asked them, Whof among yo ca recite (the Qur'an) as 'Abdulldh recite it?"" They replied"
473,"The PfOphet p.1..r,.1, ,r- fOfba offering As-Saldt (the prayer) aftt Fa.j (moming) praytill the sun ris and aftthe 'As (afternoon) prayt the sun sets. . Nanated Abuf Sa'id Al-Khud +:c dt s;s: I heard Allah's Messeng.r, rLt, ,,- saYing, There is nof Sa (prayer) aftthe morning prayer"
474,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, ""There is no prayer after the morning prayer till the sun rises, and there is no prayer after the `Asr prayer till the sun sets."""
475,"Ibn `Umar said, Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said"
476,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, When the (upper) edge of the sun appears (in the morning)"
477,"Zaid b. Thabit reported:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made an apartment with the help of the leaves of date trees or of mats. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out to pray in it. People followed him and came to pray with him. Then they again came one night and waited (for him), but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed in coming out to them. And when he did not come out, they cried aloud and threw pebbles at the door. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out in anger and said to them: By what you have been constantly doing, I was inclined to think that it (prayer) might not become obligatory for you. So you must observe prayer (optional) in your houses, for the prayer observed by a man in the house is better except an obligatory prayer"
478,"Narrated 'Aisha rri' lr - ll6h's Messengd- J.r ,- nov Preference of offering twof Rak'a befbre the Maghrib (evening) prayer"
479,"When the Mu'adhdhin pronounced the Adhdn, some of the companions of the Prophett d-J.ir, r- ll'ould proceed tof the pillars of the rnusque (fthe prayer) till the Prophett J ! i"
480,"The prophet said, There is a prayer between the two Adhans (Adhan and Iqama)"
481,Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said. While I was sleeping
482,"T Imdm stands up facing the Qiblah a one batch of them (i.e. the army) (of of the two) offers Saldt $rayer) alof with him and the othbatch faces t enemy. The Imdm offers one Rak with the first batch then th themselves stand up alone and off one bowing and twof prostrations wh they are still in thei place, and then away tof relieve the second batch, a the second batch comes (and takes t place of the first batch in the Sa behind the Imdm), and he offers t second Rak'a with them. Sof completes his twof Rak'a (with Taslim and then the second batch (gets up f the second Rak'a), bows and prostrat twof prostrations (i.e. complete the second Rak'a and thus all comple thei prayer)"
483,"This hadith has been narrated by Ibn 'Umar from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), but in the hadith transmited by Musa b. 'Uqba, this addition is made: When one who had committed the Qur'an to memory (or who is familiar with it) gets up (for night prayer) and recites it night and day"
484,Abdullah reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:What a wretched person is he amongst them who says: I have forgotten such and such a verse. (He should instead of using this expression say): I have been made to forget it. Try to remember the Qur'an for it is more apt to escape from men's minds than a hobbled camel
